faq:
  - q: What is the wash-fastness rating and expected lifespan of your prints?
    lead: Our DTF transfers are engineered to withstand repeated washing without cracking or fading, offering a lifespan that rivals the garment itself.
    a: We utilize state-of-the-art CMYK and 9-color DTF machines, along with specialized application processes, to ensure maximum washability and a premium hand feel. This durability protects your brand's image, whether you are ordering a single item or managing high-volume apparel programs.
  - q: What brand of printer, ink, and TPU powder do you use?
    lead: We exclusively use Super Garment for our DTF printers, inks, and TPU powders.
    a: Every component is rigorously quality-controlled and tested by our team to guarantee top-tier performance. By standardizing our supplies with a trusted industry leader, we ensure your custom DTF apparel receives vibrant, consistent, and long-lasting results every time.
  - q: How does Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment handle fine details, halftones, and semi-transparent gradients?
    lead: We capture the most intricate parts of your artwork using our advanced 9-color DTF machines paired with the industry's best RIP software.
    a: This technological combination ensures that fine lines, small text, and complex gradients are rendered with crisp, clean edges. Your logos and highly detailed designs will always appear sharp, accurate, and professional.
  - q: What is the hand-feel, texture, and stretchability of the final transfer?
    lead: Our DTF transfers offer a remarkably smooth texture and excellent stretchability that moves naturally with the garment.
    a: We achieve this superior hand-feel through our proprietary, rigorously tested application processes. The result is a comfortable, flexible graphic that enhances the wearer's experience without feeling heavy or rigid.
  - q: Can your DTF transfers be applied to synthetic or heat-sensitive fabrics?
    lead: Yes, our Direct-to-Film transfers are highly versatile and can be safely applied to a wide range of textiles, including synthetic and heat-sensitive fabrics.
    a: "Because we use precise, temperature-controlled equipment, our DTF technology excels on:"
    list:
      - Polyester and performance wear
      - Nylon and outerwear
      - Tri-blends and traditional cotton
  - q: Do you sell gang sheets, and what are your file setup requirements?
    lead: Yes, we provide wholesale, high-volume production of DTF gang sheets for our customers.
    a:
      - Because file requirements can vary with the complexity of your artwork, we recommend contacting our support team.
      - >-
        Please <a href="/contact-us">contact us</a> directly for detailed volume pricing, customized service options, and specific file setup guidelines.
  - q: Do you use an automated powder shaker and curing oven?
    lead: Yes, our production facility in Reno, NV utilizes fully automated powder shakers and advanced curing ovens.
    a: This automation ensures consistent, even powder application and optimal curing temperatures across every transfer. It allows us to maintain strict quality control while efficiently scaling our operations to fulfill high-volume orders without delay.
  - q: How closely can you match my brand’s CMYK or Pantone colors?
    lead: Pantone matching is our specialty, and we can match your brand's CMYK or Pantone colors with exceptional accuracy.
    a: By leveraging our industrial 9-color DTF printers and advanced RIP software, we produce brilliant, full-color graphics. This ensures your custom apparel maintains strict brand consistency across all promotional merchandise and corporate wear.
  - q: What are the minimum order quantities (MOQ) and turnaround times?
    lead: We do not require any minimum order quantities for our DTF printing services.
    a: Whether you need a single custom prototype or high-volume corporate fulfillment, our scalable systems are built to accommodate your needs. Our efficient operations ensure rapid turnaround times, delivering your products quickly without ever compromising on quality.
  - q: Do your inks and powders hold eco-friendly certifications?
    lead: Yes, the DTF inks and TPU powders we use at Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment hold eco-friendly certifications.
    a: We are committed to providing high-impact branding solutions that are safe for both the environment and your customers, ensuring your custom apparel is produced responsibly.
